Summary: Rosetta 2: refuse a program's own LDT entries, as Wine 10 did, instead of hanging
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: written for wine-mac-builds
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: Wine 11 implements NtSetLdtEntries for wow64 processes and passes the
 entry to i386_set_ldt. Rosetta 2 accepts only the entries Wine sets up
 itself (32-bit code and %fs, which don't go through NtSetLdtEntries); for
 others, such as a 16-bit data selector, it prints "rosetta error: LDT ...
 not supported" and the thread spins for ever. Wine 10's NtSetLdtEntries
 returned STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED on 64-bit macOS, and programs carried on.
 Under Rosetta, return that again.
 Seen in Bioscopia (Director 8): it stops on its first title frame after
 "rosetta error: LDT 0xf00f3210488323f not supported" (base 0x0f210488,
 limit 0x323f, 16-bit data, DPL 3).
Evidence: a 32-bit test program calling NtSetLdtEntries with that
 descriptor: on macfixes 11.22-build3 Rosetta prints the error and the
 process spins at 100% CPU; with this patch the call returns 0xc0000002
 and the program continues.
Expects before it: 0043 (is_apple_silicon)
Applies to: wine 11.21 (macfixes, after 0056)
Status: 2026-11-16: not yet built. Same change as the 11.22 patch, which was
 tested.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index ee83fc9..82240c3 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3999,6 +3999,10 @@ NTSTATUS ldt_get_entry( WORD sel, CLIENT_ID client_id, LDT_ENTRY *entry )
     return status;
 }
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+static int is_apple_silicon(void);
+#endif
+
 /******************************************************************************
  *           NtSetLdtEntries   (NTDLL.@)
  *           ZwSetLdtEntries   (NTDLL.@)
@@ -4009,6 +4013,13 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetLdtEntries( ULONG sel1, ULONG entry1_low, ULONG entry1_high
     union { LDT_ENTRY entry; ULONG ul[2]; } entry;
 
     if (is_win64 && !is_wow64()) return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    /* Rosetta 2 serves only the LDT entries Wine sets up itself (32-bit code
+     * and %fs). It stops the whole process on others, such as a program's
+     * 16-bit data selector ("rosetta error: LDT ... not supported"). Refuse
+     * them, as Wine 10 did on 64-bit macOS. */
+    if (is_apple_silicon()) return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+#endif
     if (sel1 >> 16 || sel2 >> 16) return STATUS_INVALID_LDT_DESCRIPTOR;
 
     server_enter_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
